To determine the carbohydrate content in shiitake mushrooms, 0.1 g of the extracted oven-dried sample was placed into a 10 ml test tube, followed by the addition of 5 ml of 2.5 N HCl. The mixture was incubated in a water bath for 3 h, cooled, and neutralized with Na2CO3 until effervescence ceased. The volume was adjusted to 100 ml with distilled water. Subsequently, 10 ml of this solution was centrifuged at 4000 rpm for 10 to 15 min, with a blank prepared using distilled water. Additionally, 0.1 ml of the extract was pipetted into another 10 ml test tube, and 1.9 ml of distilled water was added to make a total volume of 2 ml. To this, 4 ml of enthrone reagent was added, and the mixture was heated in a water bath at 100 °C for 8 min. After cooling, the absorbance was measured at 630 nm using a spectrophotometer [26].\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
